# The open question: does Enhanced Work Tab cohabit with Work Studio?
#
# It intercepted Pawn_WorkSettings.GetPriority during an investigation on 2026-09-19, which
# suggests it patches rather than replaces the Work tab and would therefore cohabit. That is an
# inference from one investigation, and this set is how it stops being one: the map names what to
# stage, and the run is what answers.
#
# A coexistence set, read green-is-good like the others. Green means Work Studio and Enhanced Work
# Tab live together; red means something moved and a person looks. Nothing declares this pair
# either way - neither About.xml carries an incompatibility with the other - so a red here is the
# reason to consider adding one, not a confirmation of one.
#
# Scenarios 2, 3, 7, 7b and 8 draw or click the Work tab window and are the ones that can tell.
# Scenarios 5 and 12 read priorities back, which is exactly what it intercepts, so a divergence
# there would be about the ownership of GetPriority rather than about layout.
#
# packageId read from the installed copy's own About.xml, 2026-09-21. Its only hard dependency is
# Harmony, which the staging always includes, so this file needs the one line.
#
# packageId              workshopId   what it is
natee.EnhancedWorkTab    3715873875   Enhanced Work Tab, by natee
